{{Elections in Arkansas}}

The '''2024 [[Arkansas House of Representatives]] election''' was held on November 5, 2024, alongside the [[2024 United States elections]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Arkansas House of Representatives elections, 2024 |url=https://ballotpedia.org/Arkansas_House_of_Representatives_elections,_2024 |access-date=2024-02-19 |website=Ballotpedia |language=en}}</ref>

{{toclimit|2}}

==Partisan background ==
In the 2020 Presidential Election, Republican Donald Trump won 81 of Arkansas' House districts, while Democrat Joe Biden won 19. Going into the 2024 Arkansas House Election, Democrats held one Trump-won district: District 56 in Conway (Trump +4%). Republicans held one Biden-won district: District 62, a majority African-American region in the Delta (Biden +7%).
